{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.phi_b_quasiperiod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.phi_b_quasiperiod","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.lean#L111-L128","doc":"**Quasi-periodicity under the full `ib`-shift** (the `b`-shift applied at\n`z + ib/2`):\n$$\\Phi_b(z) = \\bigl(1 + q_b\\,e^{2\\pi b z}\\bigr)\\,\\Phi_b(z + ib),\n\\qquad q_b := e^{i\\pi b^2}.$$\nThis **surfaces the modular-double parameter `q_b = e^{iπ b²}`** — the T3↔T1\nbridge datum: `q_b` is the `q` of the compact `Φ_q` (whose functional equation\n`Φ_q(q²x) = (1+qx)Φ_q(x)` is the multiplicative shadow of this additive relation\nunder `x = e^{2πbz}`, `q² = q_b`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.phi_b_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.phi_b_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.lean#L105-L109","doc":"**Ratio form of the `b`-shift** (where `Φ` does not vanish): the defining\nquotient `Φ_b(z - ib/2) / Φ_b(z + ib/2) = 1 + e^{2π b z}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.phi_binv_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.phi_binv_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.lean#L85-L103","doc":"**Ratio form of the `1/b`-shift** (the modular-dual companion of\n`phi_b_ratio`), valid off the dual pole lattice.\n\n**Removed lemma note (2026-07-11).** The earlier `phi_binv_zero` — \"wherever\n`e^{2πz/b} = −1`, `Φ(z − i/(2b)) = 0`\" — was derived from the *unguarded*\n`shift_binv` and states a **false** property of the intended `Φ_b`: at those\npoints the true `Φ_b(z − i/(2b))` is finite and non-zero, and the singular\nbehavior is a **pole** of `Φ_b` at `z + i/(2b)` (dual lattice), not a zero at\n`z − i/(2b)`.  Measured at the substrate anchor: `|Φ_b(z − i/(2b))| ≈ 1.11e−6`\nwith the `k = 0` dual product factor at `z + i/(2b)` vanishing (see the class\ndocstring).  The asymmetry with `phi_b_zero` is structural: zeros of `Φ_b`\ncome from the compact (numerator) half, poles from the dual (denominator)\nhalf; only the zero side is expressible for total functions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.phi_b_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.phi_b_zero","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.lean#L76-L83","doc":"**Derived zero locus (`b`-lattice).** From the `b`-shift axiom alone: wherever\nthe prefactor `1 + e^{2π b z}` vanishes, `Φ_b` has a zero.  This is the top edge\nof `Φ_b`'s `b`-lattice of zeros — a genuine consequence of the functional\nequation, not an assumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.FaddeevPhi.shift_binv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.FaddeevPhi.shift_binv","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.lean#L70-L70","doc":"`1/b`-shift relation (the **modular-dual** half, absent from compact\n`Φ_q`), guarded away from the dual pole lattice (see class docstring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.FaddeevPhi.shift_b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.FaddeevPhi.shift_b","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.lean#L66-L66","doc":"`b`-shift relation (the \"compact half\", same shape as `Φ_q`'s\n`q`-difference equation).  Unguarded: its prefactor zeros are genuine zeros. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.FaddeevPhi.hb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.FaddeevPhi.hb","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.lean#L63-L63","doc":"`Re b > 0` (covers real `b > 0` — the `|q| = 1` fibre regime — and the\nproduct-supported substrate branch `arg b = π/4`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.FaddeevPhi.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.FaddeevPhi.mk","kind":"ctor","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.FaddeevPhi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.FaddeevPhi","kind":"class","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm.lean#L32-L72","doc":"**Faddeev `Φ_b` (conjecture-class, §3b).** `Φ : ℂ → ℂ` satisfies the two\nmodular-double `q`-difference equations of the non-compact quantum dilogarithm\nat modular parameter `b > 0`:\n$$\\Phi_b(z - \\tfrac{ib}{2}) = \\bigl(1 + e^{2\\pi b z}\\bigr)\\,\\Phi_b(z + \\tfrac{ib}{2}),\n\\qquad\n\\Phi_b(z - \\tfrac{i}{2b}) = \\bigl(1 + e^{2\\pi z/b}\\bigr)\\,\\Phi_b(z + \\tfrac{i}{2b}).$$\nThe two relations are exchanged by `b ↔ 1/b` (with `Re (1/b) > 0` following\nfrom `Re b > 0`), encoding the **self-duality** `Φ_b = Φ_{1/b}` — the\nstructural feature the compact `Φ_q` (single relation) lacks.\n\n**Total-function encoding caveat (why `shift_binv` carries a guard).** The\ntrue `Φ_b` is meromorphic with *poles* on the `1/b`-side (dual) lattice.  At a\ndual-lattice point (`e^{2πz/b} = −1`) an unguarded relation would force\n`Φ(z − i/(2b)) = 0 · Φ(z + i/(2b)) = 0` for ANY total `Φ`, while the intended\nobject's value there is finite and non-zero — the meromorphic identity holds as\n`0 · ∞` (measured at the proton-anchor substrate `b` via the validated\nevaluator `computations/qbeta/phi_b_evaluator.py`:\n`|Φ_b(z − i/(2b))| ≈ 1.11e−6 ≠ 0` while the `k = 0` dual product factor at\n`z + i/(2b)` vanishes to `3e−34`).  An unguarded `∀ z` axiom is therefore\nunsatisfiable by any total-function encoding of `Φ_b`; the guard excludes\nexactly the dual pole lattice.  `shift_b` needs no guard: its prefactor-zero\npoints are genuine *zeros* of `Φ_b` (numerator/compact half), where\n`0 = 0 · Φ(·)` holds.\n\nThe `sorry`-free consequences below hold for *any* `Φ` in this class; the open\nconjecture is that the integral `Φ_b` **is** such a `Φ` (on the `Im b² > 0`\nsubstrate branch this is discharged by the modular-double product — see\n`QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd`; the `|q| = 1` fibre regime, real `b`, remains open). ","signatureChunk":0}]}